							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"marks": [
										{
											"type": "bold"
										}
									],
									"text": "Network automation"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": " is the process of using software to automatically deploy, configure, manage, and test network devices. It replaces slow, error-prone manual command-line configuration with programmatic, centralized control. Organizations use automation to rapidly provision services, maintain consistent security policies, and scale infrastructure without adding operational staff. Modern systems use intent-based networking tools to continuously monitor the network and automatically self-correct deviations from standard baselines. Ultimately, it shifts the role of network engineers from repetitive manual troubleshooting to writing scalable code and managing abstract architecture."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
