								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Building a network starts with gathering requirements to determine the necessary scale, budget, and required devices. Next, engineers design a hierarchical blueprint detailing the placement of hardware and the routing of cables. Technicians then physically install the routers, switches, and access points according to that layout. Once the hardware is set up, engineers configure IP addresses, routing protocols, and security rules to enable communication. Finally, rigorous testing ensures data flows smoothly, securely, and without single points of failure."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
