						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Network architecture is the blueprint that defines how devices, software, and protocols are structured to communicate. It includes both physical hardware and logical rules that guide data flow. You can learn more about its foundational setup from "
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"marks": [
										{
											"type": "link",
											"attrs": {
												"href": "https://www.cisco.com/site/us/en/learn/topics/networking/what-is-network-architecture.html",
												"target": "_blank",
												"rel": "noopener",
												"class": "H23r4e"
											}
										},
										{
											"type": "bold"
										},
										{
											"type": "underline"
										}
									],
									"text": "Cisco Systems"
								},
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": ". The two main types are peer-to-peer and client-server systems. A good design keeps data safe and fast."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
			"parentId": "page:page",
			"index": "anPtZx",
